sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Me
    participant P as codex session (gpt-5.6-sol)
    participant CS as codex security plugin (local)
    participant W as worker agents (4 to 10)
    participant GH as github
    Me->>P: "run daybreak against these repos and see what it finds"
    P->>P: read the plugin's scan workflow docs (~2 min)
    P->>GH: open a tracking issue
    P->>CS: start standard scan (returns right away)
    P->>W: spawn preflight + baseline + architecture reviewers
    P->>P: read source itself in parallel
    loop every 1 to 2 min
        W-->>P: candidate findings, threat model
    end
    P->>CS: record draft (checkpoint)
    P->>W: spawn 1 to 3 focused investigators (auth, browser, ci)
    W-->>P: focused findings
    P->>P: validate each finding against source
    P->>CS: complete scan (sealed report)
    P->>GH: comment the results on the tracking issue
    P-->>Me: summary (5 to 42 min per scan)
